      <h2 id="buying-guide">Buying Guide: How to Choose a Canva Alternative in 2026</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Step 1 — Identify your Canva limitation:</strong> Is it template depth, collaboration, data visualization, social media formats, or Adobe integration? Each alternative excels at a different gap.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 2 — Test the free tier:</strong> Adobe Express, Figma, Visme, VistaCreate, and Piktochart all have free tiers. Create one real project in each before paying.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 3 — Check team collaboration:</strong> Figma leads in real-time collaboration. Canva and Adobe Express are adequate. Visme and Piktochart are single-editor focused.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 4 — Evaluate stock assets:</strong> Adobe Express includes Adobe Stock. Canva has the largest free asset library. Others require separate stock subscriptions.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 5 — Calculate total cost:</strong> If you already pay for Creative Cloud, Adobe Express is free. Figma is $12/user/month. Compare annual costs before committing.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Learn more about our <a href="/how-we-test/">testing methodology</a> and <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>What is the best free alternative to Canva in 2026?</summary>
          <p>Adobe Express offers a free tier with access to templates, stock photos, and basic design tools, making it the best free Canva alternative for most users. VistaCreate also has a free tier with limited templates. For UI/UX design, Figma's free tier supports 3 collaborative projects. For infographics, Piktochart offers a free tier with 5 visual formats.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is Adobe Express better than Canva?</summary>
          <p>Adobe Express is better than Canva for users already in the Adobe ecosystem, because it integrates with Adobe Stock, Adobe Fonts, and Creative Cloud libraries. Canva is better for non-designers who want the largest template library and the simplest drag-and-drop experience. For teams deciding between the two, see our Canva vs Adobe Express comparison.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is Figma a good Canva alternative for marketing teams?</summary>
          <p>Figma is a good Canva alternative for marketing teams that need collaborative design with real-time multi-user editing, component systems, and design-to-dev handoff. However, Figma is a UI/UX design tool, not a template-driven marketing design tool. Marketing teams that rely on pre-built social media templates and brand kits will find Canva or Adobe Express more practical.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which Canva alternative is best for infographics?</summary>
          <p>Piktochart is the best Canva alternative for infographics and data visualization. It offers purpose-built infographic templates, chart builders, map visualizations, and data import features that Canva lacks. Visme is also strong for infographics and adds interactive charts, animated graphics, and presentation capabilities.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

